GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/starontology/skos.py> {
    ns91:skos.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.starontology.skos" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """starontology.skos

    SHACL validation of a SKOS graph against the W3C SKOS Reference's own
    numbered conditions
    (https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/). This lives here, not in
    starlayer.ontology.skos_shapes, for the same reason manch:'s manchester_validate()
    lives in starontology.manchester - validating a vocabulary against its own
    shapes is an ontology-management concern, not a starlayer.graph/.sparql one.

    Unlike ``manch:``/``srl:``, SKOS needs no encode/decode/tree layer at all -
    a SKOS thesaurus is already plain RDF the moment it's authored. So this
    module is thinner than either of those: one entry point, not four or seven.

    One entry point:

    - ``skos_validate(data_graph) -> (conforms, report_graph, report_text)`` -
      structural + the spec's own numbered conditions (S9, S13, S14,
      S19/S20, S27, S37, S46), ``skos:memberList``/``skos:member`` consistency
      (the spec's own §9.4 prose expectation, not a numbered condition), plus a
      small set of non-normative best-practice recommendations (e.g. "a Concept
      should have a prefLabel") - the latter are ``sh:severity sh:Info``, so
      they never flip ``conforms`` (``allow_infos=True`` below) - see
      ``skos_shapes.ttl``'s own per-shape comments for the full list.

    No public ``ontology_graph()``/``shapes_graph()`` here (same decision as
    ``starontology.manchester``/``starlayer.sparql.srl``) - get those two
    graphs from ``starontology`` directly instead: ``get_ontology_graph(
    "skos_owl")`` / ``get_ontology_graph("skos_shacl")``.

    **Deliberately no ``ont_graph``/``inference=ENTAILMENT.RDFS`` in
    ``skos_validate()``, unlike ``manch:``/``salg:``/``srl:``'s own** -
    ``skos-ontology.ttl``
    (the W3C's own skos.rdf) states the real spec's S19/S20 ``rdfs:domain``/``range``
    axioms, but feeding that ontology into an RDFS-inference validation pass
    would auto-entail exactly the ``skos:Concept`` type the S19/S20 shape
    exists to check for, making it tautologically vacuous (see
    ``skos_shapes.ttl``'s own module comment for the full account). Every
    shape there is written to be
    self-sufficient against the bare data graph instead - this is also why
    ``skos_validate()`` here needs no combining-with-another-vocabulary's-shapes
    logic the way ``srl.srl_validate()`` does for ``srl:``+``salg:``.""" ;
        rdfs:label "skos" ;
        ns2:declares ns93:skos_validate ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/starontology/skos.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:__future__, ns4:warnings, ns4:rdflib .

    ns93:skos_validate dcterms:identifier "starlayer.starontology.skos.skos_validate" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Validate ``data_graph`` against the shapes in ``skos_shapes.ttl``.

    Deliberately no ``ont_graph``/``inference`` - see this module's own
    docstring for why (RDFS domain/range entailment from
    ``skos-ontology.ttl``'s own faithfully-restated S19/S20 axioms would
    make the S19/S20 SHACL shape tautologically vacuous).

    Goes through ``starlayer.shacl.validate()``, never bare ``pyshacl`` -
    this validates a caller-supplied ``data_graph`` that may be genuine
    RDF 1.2 content, which only ``starlayer.shacl`` understands correctly.

    ``allow_infos=True`` is passed through unconditionally - without it,
    pyshacl's own ``conforms`` computation doesn't distinguish severity
    levels at all: an ``sh:Info``-severity result still flips ``conforms``
    to ``False`` by default. Without this, the best-practice shapes in
    ``skos_shapes.ttl`` (``sh:severity sh:Info``) would make an otherwise
    entirely valid thesaurus that merely skips a recommendation report
    ``conforms == False`` - defeating the entire point of using
    ``sh:Info`` instead of the default ``sh:Violation``.""" ;
        rdfs:label "skos_validate" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/starontology/skos.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns93:skos_validate.param.data_graph ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns93:skos_validate.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 95 ;
        ns2:lineStart 53 ;
        ns2:signature "def skos_validate(data_graph: Graph) -> tuple[bool, Graph, str]" .

    ns93:skos_validate.param.data_graph a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "Any SKOS thesaurus - hand-authored, parsed from RDF/XML or Turtle, whatever." ;
        rdfs:label "data_graph" ;
        ns2:annotationText "Graph" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:rdflib.graph.Graph ;
        ns2:parameterKind "positional" ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns93:skos_validate.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        rdfs:comment "``(conforms, results_graph, results_text)``, unpacked from ``starlayer.shacl``'s own ``ValidationResult``." ;
        ns2:annotationText "tuple[bool, Graph, str]" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.bool, ns4:builtins.str, ns4:rdflib.graph.Graph, ns4:builtins.tuple .

    ns4:__future__ a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns4:builtins.bool dcterms:identifier "builtins.bool" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "bool" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:builtins.str dcterms:identifier "builtins.str" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "str" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:builtins.tuple dcterms:identifier "builtins.tuple" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "tuple" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:rdflib a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns4:rdflib.graph.Graph dcterms:identifier "rdflib.graph.Graph" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "Graph" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:warnings a ns2:ExternalModule .
}

