GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/graph/shape_derivation.py> {
    ns25:shape_derivation.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.graph.shape_derivation" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """starlayer.graph.graph.shape_derivation

    ``StarLayerGraph.derive_shape()`` - infer a SHACL shape from a graph's own data:
    one ``sh:NodeShape`` per distinct ``rdf:type`` found (never per-node or
    heuristic clustering - the simplest option, per the design this follows),
    optionally reconciled against an existing template shape. See the approved
    plan (`future_enhancements.md`'s shape-derivation SUGGESTION item) for the
    full design rationale - summarized here, not re-derived.

    **Always goes through ``starlayer.shacl``, never bare ``pyshacl``.** The data or a
    template shape may be genuine RDF 1.2 content (triple terms) that only
    ``starlayer.shacl`` understands - this is why `packages/graph` depends on
    `packages/shacl` at all (an intentional circular dependency with
    `starlayer.sparql`'s own `graph`<->`sparql` cycle as direct precedent, not a
    layering mistake). The actual ``import starlayer.shacl`` stays lazy, inside the
    functions that need it, to avoid a circular *Python* import at interpreter
    load time now that the package dependency graph has a real cycle - the same
    "import order matters" caution `starlayer.sparql`'s own `CLAUDE.md` documents for
    its existing cycle with `starlayer.graph`.

    Two phases:

    - **Phase A (fresh derivation)** - always runs; the whole algorithm when no
      template is given. Pure RDF graph analysis, no SHACL validation needed at
      all (only a final self-check, see below).
    - **Phase B (template merge)** - only when a template shape is given. Runs
      ``starlayer.shacl.validate()`` once to detect every violation, then dispatches
      each one by its ``sh:sourceConstraintComponent``: constraint types with a
      principled data-driven fix get recomputed from the *true* current data
      (not just patched around the one violating value); constraint types with
      no generic fix (``sh:pattern``, cross-property comparisons, opaque
      ``sh:sparql``/custom components) are either dropped-with-a-comment or, for
      the opaque case, left untouched-with-a-comment - see
      ``_RECOMPUTE_COMPONENTS``/``_DROP_COMPONENTS`` below for the exact table.

    Value-kind analysis (Phase A step 3, reused by Phase B's recompute/extend
    paths) recognizes four first-class kinds, not three: ``Literal``,
    ``URIRef``, ``BNode``, and **``TripleTerm``** - SHACL 1.2 has a real,
    already-implemented node kind for this (``sh:nodeKind sh:TripleTerm``,
    list-valued too, e.g. ``sh:nodeKind ( sh:IRI sh:TripleTerm )`` for a
    mixed-kind property - see ``starlayer.shacl/native_components.py``'s
    ``_build_node_kind_component()``), so a triple-term-valued property must
    never be silently dropped from the derived shape.

    Both phases end with a **self-check**: run the derived/merged shape back
    through ``starlayer.shacl.validate()`` against the same data. Phase A's result
    must conform unconditionally - if it doesn't, that's a bug in this module,
    not an expected outcome. Phase B's result must conform except at whatever
    opaque (``sh:sparql``/custom-component) violations were deliberately left
    untouched - anything else still failing is likewise a bug here.""" ;
        rdfs:label "shape_derivation" ;
        ns2:declares ns27:_class_predicates, ns27:_owning_target_class, ns27:_close_shape, ns27:_derive_class_shape, ns27:_build_rdf_list, ns27:_self_check, ns27:_clear_list_valued, ns27:_extend_new_properties_and_classes, ns27:_recompute_component, ns27:_derive_fresh, ns27:_term_kind, ns27:_shared_rdf_type, ns27:_remove_rdf_list, ns27:_annotate_opaque, ns27:_derive_with_template, ns27:derive_shape, ns27:_literal_datatype_bucket, ns27:_carry_forward_ignored_properties, ns27:_close_all_node_shapes, ns27:_drop_and_annotate, ns27:_set_node_kind_constraints, ns27:_iter_violations, ns27:_derive_property_shape ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/graph/shape_derivation.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:__future__, ns4:rdflib.collection, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:rdflib .

    ns27:_annotate_opaque dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.graph.shape_derivation._annotate_opaque" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:label "_annotate_opaque" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/graph/shape_derivation.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns27:_annotate_opaque.param.working, ns27:_annotate_opaque.param.component, ns27:_annotate_opaque.param.shape_node ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns27:_annotate_opaque.returns ;
        ns2:isPrivate true ;
        ns2:lineEnd 482 ;
        ns2:lineStart 476 ;
        ns2:signature "def _annotate_opaque(working: Graph, shape_node, component) -> None" .

    ns27:_annotate_opaque.param.component a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "component" ;
        ns2:parameterKind "positional" ;
        ns2:position 2 .

    ns27:_annotate_opaque.param.shape_node a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "shape_node" ;
        ns2:parameterKind "positional" ;
        ns2:position 1 .

    ns27:_annotate_opaque.param.working a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "working" ;
