GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/graph/integration/test_sqlalchemy_backend.py> {
    ns155:test_sqlalchemy_backend.py dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.integration.test_sqlalchemy_backend" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """tests/integration/test_sqlalchemy_backend.py

    Integration tests for StarLayerGraph backed by a real on-disk SQLite
    database via rdflib-sqlalchemy (backend='rdf-1.1' - rdflib-sqlalchemy has
    no RDF 1.2 native mode, so only the encoding-based backend applies here).

    Permanent pytest coverage for a StarLayerGraph backed by a real on-disk
    SQLite store, plus regression coverage for the custom SPARQL functions
    (TRIPLE()/isTRIPLE()/SUBJECT()/PREDICATE()/OBJECT()/STRLANGDIR()) confirmed
    this session to already work correctly against this store: unlike a genuinely
    remote SPARQLStore/SPARQLUpdateStore endpoint (Fuseki-as-1.1), the SQLAlchemy
    store accepts a pre-parsed rdflib Query object
    (starlayer.graph.query.query_cache.store_accepts_prepared_query returns True for
    it), so queries are evaluated locally, in-process, where starlayer.graph's custom
    function registrations are visible - no decomposition needed. These tests
    exist to keep that fact pinned down, not to fix a bug.

    Requires the `sqlalchemy` extra: pip install -e ".[sqlalchemy]"

    Run:
        .venv/bin/pytest tests/integration/test_sqlalchemy_backend.py -v""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_sqlalchemy_backend" ;
        ns2:declares ns263:TestSQLAlchemySPARQL, ns263:TestSQLAlchemyRoundTrip, ns263:db_path, ns263:sg, ns263:TestSQLAlchemySparqlFunctions, ns263:_reopen ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/integration/test_sqlalchemy_backend.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:os, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:pytest, ns4:rdflib, ns4:tempfile, ns4:rdflib_sqlalchemy .

