GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/starontology/manchester_conformance/test_mc_shapes_mutation.py> {
    ns334:test_mc_shapes_mutation.py dcterms:identifier "tests.starontology.manchester_conformance.test_mc_shapes_mutation" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Can the shapes tell a broken ``manch:`` tree from a good one?

    Passing every valid tree (test_mc_tree.py) only shows the shapes are not too strict. This file checks they
    are not too lax: take valid trees, damage them in ways a hand- or LLM-authored tree could be damaged, and
    require ``manchester_validate`` to reject them.

    The first run of a full mutation scan (``tools/mutation_scan.py``: 430 mutants, one per distinct
    (node class, property, operator) in the corpus) found 10 trees that PASSED validation yet crash the
    decoder, and a list shape that accepted unterminated and cyclic lists. Both are fixed; these tests keep
    them fixed. The cause of the first: validation runs with RDFS inference, several ``manch:`` properties
    declare an ``rdfs:domain``, so a deleted ``rdf:type`` was inferred straight back and every shape was
    satisfied - the decoder, reading asserted types, was not. ``manchester_validate`` now has a pre-flight
    check on the asserted graph.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_mc_shapes_mutation" ;
        ns2:declares ns336:test_dropping_the_type_of_any_node_class_is_caught, ns336:test_every_single_triple_removal_that_validates_still_decodes, ns336:_trees_of_the_corpus, ns336:_cells, ns336:test_a_tree_with_no_document_is_rejected, ns336:_head_of, ns336:test_the_report_graph_carries_the_preflight_findings, ns336:test_a_cyclic_list_is_rejected, ns336:test_an_unterminated_list_is_rejected, ns336:test_the_unmutated_tree_conforms, ns336:test_a_list_item_of_the_wrong_kind_is_rejected, ns336:test_two_documents_are_rejected, ns336:_tree, ns336:test_an_unknown_manch_type_is_rejected ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/starontology/manchester_conformance/test_mc_shapes_mutation.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:pytest, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:__future__, ns4:rdflib .

