GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/version_directive.py> {
    ns33:version_directive.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.version_directive" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """SPARQL 1.2 Query prologue's optional ``VERSION "label"`` directive
    (SPARQL 1.2 Query sec 4.3), e.g. the spec's own example::

        VERSION "1.2"
        PREFIX : <http://example/>
        SELECT ...

    Not real SPARQL 1.1 syntax at all — rdflib's parser (and
    ``starlayer.sparql``'s own grammar, which extends it) has no notion of this
    directive and raises a ``ParseException`` on it unconditionally, so it must
    always be stripped before ordinary parsing, regardless of pipeline or
    backend.

    **``VERSION`` is not always the first token.** Per the real grammar
    (``tests/graph/vendor/spec_snapshots/sparql12-query.txt``):
    ``Prologue ::= ( BaseDecl | PrefixDecl | VersionDecl )*`` - the three
    prologue declaration kinds may appear in *any* order and ``VersionDecl`` may
    appear more than once. That's why this module scans the whole leading
    prologue token-by-token (recognizing ``BaseDecl``/``PrefixDecl`` well enough
    to skip over them unmodified, removing only ``VersionDecl`` tokens wherever
    they appear) rather than anchor-matching ``VERSION`` as the very first
    token of the document, which the grammar does not guarantee.

    Kept as its own small, self-contained module (not part of the retired
    ``sparql12_to_11.py`` text rewriter it used to live in): a prologue-only
    token scan has none of the nested/ambiguous-structure fragility (ordering-
    sensitive splicing, join-order bugs) that motivated replacing the rest of
    that module with a real grammar/algebra pipeline — there's no *query body*
    structure to get wrong here, only the three known prologue declaration
    shapes to recognize and either pass through (``BaseDecl``/``PrefixDecl``) or
    remove (``VersionDecl``).

    See ``starlayer.graph.model.conformance`` for what happens with the extracted
    label (a warning, never a hard error, if it doesn't match what the query
    actually uses), and ``starlayer.graph.backends.native.check_native_version_conformance``
    for the equivalent used by the native rdf-1.2 backend, which sends VERSION
    straight through to the endpoint unmodified instead of stripping it.""" ;
        rdfs:label "version_directive" ;
        ns2:declares ns41:contains_triple_term, ns41:strip_version_directive ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/version_directive.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:__future__, ns4:re .

    ns41:contains_triple_term dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.version_directive.contains_triple_term" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Recursively check whether a parsed SPARQL 1.2 parse tree/algebra
    contains a ``TripleTermNode`` anywhere — used for VERSION-directive
    conformance checking (see ``starlayer.graph.model.conformance``). More
    reliable than a text-presence heuristic: this walks the real parsed
    structure, so it can't be fooled by e.g. ``<<(`` appearing inside a
    string literal or comment.""" ;
        rdfs:label "contains_triple_term" ;
        ns2:calls ns41:contains_triple_term ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/version_directive.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns41:contains_triple_term.param.node ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns41:contains_triple_term.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 122 ;
        ns2:lineStart 97 ;
        ns2:signature "def contains_triple_term(node) -> bool" .

    ns41:contains_triple_term.param.node a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "A parse tree/algebra node, list, tuple, or leaf value to search." ;
        rdfs:label "node" ;
        ns2:parameterKind "positional" ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns41:contains_triple_term.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        rdfs:comment "True if a ``TripleTermNode`` appears anywhere in ``node``." ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.bool .

    ns41:strip_version_directive dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.version_directive.strip_version_directive" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Strip every ``VERSION "label"`` directive out of the leading
    prologue, leaving any ``BASE``/``PREFIX`` declarations - and their
    original relative order - untouched.

    If more than one ``VersionDecl`` is present (legal per the grammar's own
    ``( ... )*``, though the spec gives no precedence rule for it), the
    *last* one scanned is returned - an arbitrary but documented choice for
    a case real queries are not expected to actually use.""" ;
        rdfs:label "strip_version_directive" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/version_directive.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns41:strip_version_directive.param.query ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns41:strip_version_directive.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 94 ;
        ns2:lineStart 56 ;
        ns2:signature "def strip_version_directive(query: str) -> tuple[str, str | None]" .

    ns41:strip_version_directive.param.query a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "The raw SPARQL 1.2 query/update text, possibly carrying one or more leading ``VERSION`` directives." ;
        rdfs:label "query" ;
        ns2:annotationText "str" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        ns2:parameterKind "positional" ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns41:strip_version_directive.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        rdfs:comment "A ``(stripped_query, label)`` tuple: the query text with every ``VersionDecl`` removed, and the declared version label, or ``None`` if no ``VERSION`` directive was present." ;
        ns2:annotationText "tuple[str, str | None]" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.str, ns4:builtins.tuple .

    ns4:__future__ a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns4:builtins.bool dcterms:identifier "builtins.bool" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "bool" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:builtins.str dcterms:identifier "builtins.str" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "str" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:builtins.tuple dcterms:identifier "builtins.tuple" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "tuple" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:re a ns2:ExternalModule .
}

GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/sparql/serialize12.py> {
    ns48:serialize12.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.sparql.serialize12" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Serialize a SPARQL 1.2 algebra tree (with ``TripleTermNode`` nodes) back
    into SPARQL 1.2 query text — the counterpart to ``parse12.py``.

    Extends rdflib's own ``algebra.translateAlgebra``/``_AlgebraTranslator``,
    which already turns an ordinary (SPARQL-1.1-shaped) algebra tree back into
    query text, in these ways:

    1. ``BGP``/``TriplesBlock`` (the latter used for CONSTRUCT templates) call
       ``.n3()`` directly on each triple-pattern term rather than delegating
       through ``convert_node_arg``/child traversal the way most other
       operators do. ``CompValue`` (and therefore ``TripleTermNode``) has no
       ``.n3()`` method, so both branches are overridden to render a
       ``TripleTermNode`` as ``<<( s p o )>>`` instead of crashing with
       ``AttributeError``.
    2. ``Builtin_isTRIPLE``/``SUBJECT``/``PREDICATE``/``OBJECT`` and
       ``Builtin_LANGDIR``/``hasLANGDIR``/``hasLANG``/``STRLANGDIR`` are new
       SPARQL 1.2 builtins rdflib has no branch for at all — added following
       the same pattern as any other builtin (e.g. ``Builtin_STR`` for the
       single-argument ones, ``Builtin_STRLANG`` for the three-argument one).
    3. ``ConstructQuery`` and ``AskQuery`` are **new capabilities**, not a
       patch to an existing branch: plain, unmodified rdflib has no case for
       either — ``translateAlgebra`` returns an empty string for both query
       forms even with zero triple terms involved, since
       ``self._alg_translation`` is only ever seeded by the ``SelectQuery``
       branch. Two non-obvious things apply to both: (a) ``node.p`` (a
       ``Project`` wrapping the WHERE pattern) can't be referenced the way
       ``SelectQuery`` does — for CONSTRUCT/ASK, ``Project.PV`` is internal
       bookkeeping (which variables the template needs, or every variable the
       pattern mentions), not "the variable list to print after SELECT", but
       the base class's ``Project`` branch doesn't know that distinction and
       prints it anyway, producing invalid syntax — fixed by referencing
       ``node.p.p`` directly, skipping ``Project``'s own branch entirely; (b)
       for CONSTRUCT specifically, the literal ``WHERE`` keyword is included
       explicitly even though it's optional per the SPARQL grammar itself
       (rdflib's own ``WhereClause`` production is
       ``Optional(Keyword("WHERE")) + ...``) — required for compatibility with
       *starlayer.graph's* own SPARQL-1.2-to-1.1 rewriter, a regex-based,
       non-full-grammar-parsing tool that needs the keyword present even
       though plain rdflib re-parses a WHERE-less CONSTRUCT without complaint.

    Everything else is inherited from ``_AlgebraTranslator`` completely
    unchanged.

    Scope: Query algebra only (``SELECT``/``CONSTRUCT``/``ASK``), matching
    this project's existing ``translateAlgebra`` usage — Update algebra is
    never serialized back to text by this project (see
    ``test_phase2_update.py``'s docstring: "this project doesn't attempt to
    serialize Update algebra back to text at all"). ``DESCRIBE`` is still
    unsupported — the same "no branch, nothing ever seeds
    ``self._alg_translation``" gap applies to it too, not pursued since
    nothing in this project's scope currently needs it. A ``VALUES`` row
    containing a triple-term *value* (as opposed to a triple term appearing in
    an ordinary triple pattern) is handled too — see the ``values`` branch
    below.""" ;
        rdfs:label "serialize12" ;
        ns2:declares ns70:_dirlang_n3, ns70:_term_text, ns70:_triples_text, ns70:_AlgebraTranslator12, ns70:_translate_algebra_12 ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/sparql/serialize12.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:__future__, ns4:rdflib.plugins.sparql.algebra, ns4:rdflib.plugins.sparql.parserutils, ns4:rdflib.plugins.sparql.sparql, ns4:rdflib.term .

