    ns119:TestDefaultValueFallback dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_values.TestDefaultValueFallback" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """sh:defaultValue: the third step of SHACL 1.2 Core's own "Value Nodes
    of Property Shapes" algorithm - "if the set is still empty and d is the
    value of sh:defaultValue ..., then add the output nodes of
    evalExpr(d, ...)" - the only one of the three steps that's conditional.

    Found missing entirely (2026-09-09) by trying to write a notebook demo
    for it: this file's own module docstring, and
    ``_patch_shape_value_nodes_for_sh_values``'s docstring in validator.py,
    both already quoted this exact three-step algorithm - but the patch
    itself only ever implemented steps 1 and 2 (path values, sh:values),
    never step 3. A live check (a property shape with sh:defaultValue and
    sh:hasValue matching it, and no stored value at all) confirmed
    validate() reported a violation instead of conforming - a real,
    previously-undetected gap between the documented algorithm and the
    actual code, not merely an absent example.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestDefaultValueFallback" ;
        ns2:declares ns119:TestDefaultValueFallback.test_default_value_alone_with_no_sh_values_at_all_still_falls_back, ns119:TestDefaultValueFallback.test_default_value_fills_in_when_no_real_value_is_stored, ns119:TestDefaultValueFallback.test_default_value_is_ignored_once_a_real_value_exists, ns119:TestDefaultValueFallback.test_default_value_is_ignored_once_sh_values_computes_something ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_values.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 224 ;
        ns2:lineStart 122 .

    ns119:TestDefaultValueFallback.test_default_value_alone_with_no_sh_values_at_all_still_falls_back dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_values.TestDefaultValueFallback.test_default_value_alone_with_no_sh_values_at_all_still_falls_back" ;
        a ns2:Method ;
        rdfs:comment """The gate must trigger on sh:defaultValue alone, not just when
    sh:values is also present - a plain property shape carrying only
    sh:defaultValue (the common, simpler case) needs the same fallback.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_default_value_alone_with_no_sh_values_at_all_still_falls_back" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_values.py" ;
