GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/sqe_coverage/test_sqe_shape_mutations.py> {
    ns319:test_sqe_shape_mutations.py dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.sqe_coverage.test_sqe_shape_mutations" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Adversarial audit of the sqe shapes: take rich, valid trees, corrupt one property at a time (remove it,
    replace its value with a junk literal, add a second value) and require the shapes to notice.

    Some corruptions are legitimately valid and are listed here, with the reason:

    * removing an optional property (modifiers, ``sqe:negated``, prefixes, ...);
    * a string literal where an expression operand is expected - a literal is a valid SPARQL operand;
    * a literal as the object of a triple pattern or triple term - a valid RDF term;
    * ``sqe:prologuePrefix`` / ``sqe:values`` ... repeated or removed - a query may declare many prefixes.

    Opt-in (``pytest --sqe-coverage``); about 5 minutes.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_sqe_shape_mutations" ;
        ns2:declares ns325:_mutations, ns325:test_corruption_is_noticed_unless_it_is_legitimately_valid, ns325:_local ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/sqe_coverage/test_sqe_shape_mutations.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:rdflib, ns4:pytest .

