GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/graph/_rdflib_inherited_contract.py> {
    ns25:_rdflib_inherited_contract.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.graph._rdflib_inherited_contract" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """A recorded snapshot of every plain-rdflib method and property
    ``StarLayerGraph``/``StarLayerDataset`` inherit **unchanged** - never
    overridden anywhere in this project's own code, reaching a caller purely
    via Python's normal inheritance.

    **Why this exists.** Relying on plain inheritance for these methods is the
    right call (duplicating ~38 method bodies as do-nothing wrappers just to
    "be explicit" would mean manually tracking every future rdflib signature
    change forever, for methods this project doesn't actually modify - a real,
    ongoing maintenance cost for no behavioral benefit). But "we accept
    whatever rdflib gives us here" shouldn't mean "we never notice if that
    changes." This file is the deliberate, written-down record of what we
    currently know about each one - consumed two ways:

    1. ``tests/graph/unit/test_rdflib_inherited_contract.py`` re-introspects
       each entry's real, live signature on every test run and asserts it
       still matches ``signature`` below - a future rdflib upgrade that
       changes one of these (renamed/reordered/added parameter, changed
       return type) fails loudly and visibly, forcing a deliberate update to
       this file, rather than ``docs/working/archive/api-reference.md`` silently going stale.
    2. ``docs/working/archive/api-reference.md``'s generation step reads ``returns`` from here
       to populate the Returns column for these rows - most of rdflib's own
       methods already carry a real return-type annotation (introspectable
       directly, no need to duplicate it here), but a few genuinely don't
       (``transitiveClosure`` - see its own entry below) and need a
       hand-derived value recorded once, by a human who actually read the
       source.

    **Scope**: only the ``Unchanged`` rows in the ``StarLayerGraph``/
    ``StarLayerDataset`` member tables - i.e. methods this project's own code
    never touches. ``New``/``Modified`` methods are StarLayer's own code and
    should carry real type annotations at their own definition site instead of
    being recorded here - that's a separate, still-open piece of work (adding
    annotations to ``starlayer_graph.py``/``starlayer_dataset.py``'s own
    method definitions), not something this file is meant to stand in for.

    **Recorded against**: rdflib 7.x, as installed when this file was last
    updated (2026-10-02). If the drift test ever fails, don't just paste in
    the new signature and move on - check *why* it changed (a real behavior
    change vs. a cosmetic typing update) before updating the entry.""" ;
        rdfs:label "_rdflib_inherited_contract" ;
        ns2:declares ns29:InheritedMethodContract, ns29:InheritedPropertyContract ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/graph/_rdflib_inherited_contract.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:dataclasses, ns4:__future__ .

    ns29:InheritedMethodContract dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.graph._rdflib_inherited_contract.InheritedMethodContract" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """One inherited-and-unchanged method's recorded signature/return type.

    ``owner`` names which class (``"StarLayerGraph"`` or
    ``"StarLayerDataset"``) the drift test should introspect - for a method
    present on both with the exact same underlying function object (true
    for most of these; confirmed live), it doesn't matter which one is
    checked. For the few where StarLayerGraph *does* override the method
    (``isomorphic`` - Modified on Graph, but still plain-inherited on
    Dataset), ``owner`` deliberately points at ``StarLayerDataset``, the
    genuinely-unchanged occurrence. (``cbd`` and ``triples_choices`` used
    to be examples here too, until StarLayerDataset got its own
    overrides for each - see those methods' own docstrings for the real
    bugs that motivated them. No longer anything to record in this file.)""" ;
        rdfs:label "InheritedMethodContract" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/graph/_rdflib_inherited_contract.py" ;
        ns2:hasAttribute ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.returns, ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.owner, ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.signature, ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.hand_authored_returns ;
        ns2:hasDecorator ns29:InheritedMethodContract.decorator.0 ;
        ns2:lineEnd 68 ;
        ns2:lineStart 49 .

    ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.hand_authored_returns a ns2:Attribute ;
        rdfs:label "hand_authored_returns" ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:defaultValue "False" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.bool ;
        ns2:position 3 .

    ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.owner a ns2:Attribute ;
        rdfs:label "owner" ;
        ns2:annotationText "str" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.returns a ns2:Attribute ;
        rdfs:label "returns" ;
        ns2:annotationText "str" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        ns2:position 2 .

    ns29:InheritedMethodContract.attr.signature a ns2:Attribute ;
        rdfs:label "signature" ;
        ns2:annotationText "str" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        ns2:position 1 .

    ns29:InheritedMethodContract.decorator.0 a ns2:Decorator ;
        ns2:decoratorText "dataclass(frozen=True)" ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns29:InheritedPropertyContract dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.graph._rdflib_inherited_contract.InheritedPropertyContract" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """One inherited-and-unchanged property's recorded return type.

    No ``signature`` field (a property takes no arguments by definition -
    there's nothing to drift there beyond whether it still exists), just
    ``returns``, keyed by ``(owner, name)`` since - unlike most of the
    methods above - ``identifier`` genuinely has a *different* underlying
    function per class (``StarLayerDataset.identifier`` is rdflib's own
    deprecation-warning wrapper around ``StarLayerGraph.identifier``'s
    value, confirmed live: different ``fget`` objects, and accessing it on
    a ``Dataset`` actually emits a ``DeprecationWarning`` at runtime).
    ``deprecated`` records that distinction so the drift test (and anyone
    reading this file) doesn't mistake the two for identical.""" ;
        rdfs:label "InheritedPropertyContract" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/graph/_rdflib_inherited_contract.py" ;
        ns2:hasAttribute ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.attr.hand_authored_returns, ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.attr.returns, ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.attr.deprecated ;
        ns2:hasDecorator ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.decorator.0 ;
        ns2:lineEnd 89 ;
        ns2:lineStart 72 .

    ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.attr.deprecated a ns2:Attribute ;
        rdfs:label "deprecated" ;
        ns2:annotationText "str | None" ;
        ns2:defaultValue "None" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        ns2:optional true ;
        ns2:position 2 .

    ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.attr.hand_authored_returns a ns2:Attribute ;
        rdfs:label "hand_authored_returns" ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:defaultValue "False" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.bool ;
        ns2:position 1 .

    ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.attr.returns a ns2:Attribute ;
        rdfs:label "returns" ;
        ns2:annotationText "str" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns29:InheritedPropertyContract.decorator.0 a ns2:Decorator ;
        ns2:decoratorText "dataclass(frozen=True)" ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns4:__future__ a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns4:builtins.bool dcterms:identifier "builtins.bool" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "bool" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:builtins.str dcterms:identifier "builtins.str" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "str" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns4:dataclasses a ns2:ExternalModule .
}

GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/turtle_parser.py> {
    ns11:turtle_parser.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.turtle_parser" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """starlayer.graph.parsers.turtle_parser

    Parses Turtle 1.2 text into an rdflib.Graph, expanding RDF 1.2 quoted-triple
    syntax (<<( )>>, << >>, {| |}, ~ reifier) into the starlayer.graph internal encoding:

      Triple terms  → content-addressed URIRefs under tt: namespace
      Anon reifiers → plain BNodes (anonymous by nature)
      Named reifiers → unchanged (already named URIs)

    Entry point: StarLayerTurtleParser().parse(data)""" ;
        rdfs:label "turtle_parser" ;
        ns2:declares ns14:_to_node, ns14:_strip_blank_and_comment_lines, ns14:_get_reifier_parts, ns14:_Expander, ns14:_has_reifier, ns14:decode_tt_encoded_triples, ns14:_is_qt_reif, ns14:_is_bnode_list, ns14:_unescape, ns14:_norm_qt, ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser, ns14:_is_qt, ns14:_is_qt_term, ns14:_skolemize_encoding, ns14:_split_literal ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/turtle_parser.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:urllib.parse, ns4:secrets, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:rdflib, ns4:re .

    ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.turtle_parser.StarLayerTurtleParser" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:label "StarLayerTurtleParser" ;
        ns2:declares ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/turtle_parser.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 1157 ;
        ns2:lineStart 986 .

    ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.turtle_parser.StarLayerTurtleParser.parse" ;
        a ns2:Method ;
        rdfs:comment """Parse Turtle 1.2 text and return an rdflib.Graph.

    The graph uses the starlayer.graph internal blank-node encoding for RDF 1.2
    triple terms and reification. Pass debug=True to print intermediate
    representations to stdout.

    base seeds relative-IRI resolution (including a bare "<>") before any
    parsing happens, the same role rdflib's own parsers give their
    publicID/base argument - an in-document @base/BASE directive, if
    present, still overrides it from that point on (current_base is
    reassigned, not merged). Previously there was no way to seed this at
    all from the caller; a document with no @base of its own had no
    working relative-IRI resolution regardless of what publicID the
    caller (e.g. StarLayerGraph.parse(location=..., publicID=...))
    passed in - confirmed via the W3C SHACL 1.2 test suite, whose
    manifest files rely pervasively on "<>" self-reference.""" ;
        rdfs:label "parse" ;
        ns2:calls ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line, ns18:extract_fields, ns18:expand_triple_set, ns18:classify_statement, ns18:split_statements_with_lines, ns14:_to_node, ns14:_strip_blank_and_comment_lines ;
        ns2:declares ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/turtle_parser.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse.param.base, ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse.param.data, ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse.param.debug ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse.returns ;
        ns2:instantiates ns14:_Expander ;
        ns2:lineEnd 1157 ;
        ns2:lineStart 988 ;
        ns2:signature "def parse(self, data: str, debug: bool=False, base: str=None) -> Graph" .

    ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.turtle_parser.StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:label "_orig_line" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/turtle_parser.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line.param.cleaned_line ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line.returns ;
        ns2:isPrivate true ;
        ns2:lineEnd 1032 ;
        ns2:lineStart 1028 ;
        ns2:signature "def _orig_line(cleaned_line: int) -> int" .

    ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line.param.cleaned_line a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "cleaned_line" ;
        ns2:annotationText "int" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.int ;
        ns2:parameterKind "positional" ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse._orig_line.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "int" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:builtins.int .

    ns14:StarLayerTurtleParser.parse.param.base a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "The base IRI to seed relative-IRI resolution with before parsing begins; an in-document @base/BASE directive still overrides it from that point on." ;
        rdfs:label "base" ;
